WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.630
Seal some gas in a rigid flask.

2
00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:04.690
Its volume can't change.

3
00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:07.040
Warm it, and the pressure climbs.

4
00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:09.560
Cool it, and the pressure falls.

5
00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:14.830
Measure the pressure at several temperatures
between 0 and 100 degrees Celsius.

6
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.400
The points lie on a straight line.

7
00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:20.990
Now keep cooling, far beyond
anything you measured.

8
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.970
At what temperature would
the pressure reach zero?

9
00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:27.220
In this mission, you'll
meet the ideal gas equation,

10
00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:31.510
linking pressure, volume,
temperature and the amount of gas.

11
00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:36.500
Then you'll warm a sealed cylinder of
helium from 20 to 60 degrees Celsius,

12
00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:38.540
and predict its new pressure.

13
00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:42.920
Your mission: find out the temperature
at which the pressure would reach zero.
